    "summary": "Fiery Set with Alligator→Other One and tight Not Fade Away",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a scorching Alligator into The Other One segue, an inspired Attics Of My Life, and a rousing Not Fade Away encore. Jerry’s lead work is melodic and mind‑melded while the rhythm section drives the energy despite some snare issues.",
    "review": "July 10 1970 at the Fillmore East captures the Dead in peak ’70 form. The first set roars out of the gate with a crisp Cold Rain And Snow before diving into an incendiary Alligator → The Other One transition that feels like pure improvisational fire. Attics Of My Life follows, giving Pigpen’s lyrical storytelling a soaring backdrop while the twin drummers keep a propulsive pulse—though Mickey’s snare is a bit loose on this tape. The night rolls to a satisfying close with a Not Fade Away encore where Jerry’s lead work hits that ‘mind‑meld’ sweet spot, leaving the audience buzzing. While the recording is an audience capture with hallway ambience and occasional muddiness, it remains a listenable snapshot of a band locked in, making it a must‑hear for fans of this era.",
